  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Ace Start**: As soon as an Ace appears in the tableau or from the stock, move it to the foundation area.\n2. **Building**: You can move a card from the Tableau to the Foundations if it is the next card in sequence and same suit (e.g., 8 on 7, 9 on 8... Jack on 10).\n3. **Reserve**: If a space is cleared in the Tableau, it is immediately filled by the top card of the Stock.\n4. **The Draw**: When no more moves are possible in the Tableau, deal cards from the stock one by one to see if they can be played to the foundations or placed in an empty tableau spot.',
    Player: '1. **Ace Start**: As soon as an Ace appears in the tableau or from the stock, move it to the foundation area.\n2. **Building**: You can move a card from the Tableau to the Foundations if it is the next card in sequence and same suit (e.g., 8 on 7, 9 on 8... Jack on 10).\n3. **Reserve**: If a space is cleared in the Tableau, it is immediately filled by the top card of the Stock.\n4. **The Draw**: When no more moves are possible in the Tableau, deal cards from the stock one by one to see if they can be played to the foundations or placed in an empty tableau spot.',
    objective: 'Build four foundation piles by suit, from Ace up to King.',
    gameplay: '1. **Ace Start**: As soon as an Ace appears in the tableau or from the stock, move it to the foundation area.\n2. **Building**: You can move a card from the Tableau to the Foundations if it is the next card in sequence and same suit (e.g., 8 on 7, 9 on 8... Jack on 10).\n3. **Reserve**: If a space is cleared in the Tableau, it is immediately filled by the top card of the Stock.\n4. **The Draw**: When no more moves are possible in the Tableau, deal cards from the stock one by one to see if they can be played to the foundations or placed in an empty tableau spot.',
    keyRules: [
      'Aces move to foundation as soon as they appear in tableau or from stock.',
      'Build foundations in same suit ascending (7 on Ace, 8 on 7, through King).',
      'Empty tableau slot is filled immediately from the top of the stock.',
      'When no moves are possible, turn cards from the stock one at a time; each may be played to foundation or to an empty tableau slot.',
    ],
